cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PyEXPINT in research, please cite this software release and its associated publication when available."
title: "PyEXPINT: backend-independent exponential integrators in Python"
type: software
license: MIT
version: "0.9.0"
date-released: 2026-09-17
repository-code: "https://github.com/FrancisRVillatoro/pyexpint"
abstract: >-
  PyEXPINT is a Python framework for exponential Runge--Kutta, multistep,
  and general-linear integrators with interchangeable matrix-function-action
  backends, backend-aware work instrumentation, and reproducible benchmarking
  tools for problem- and hardware-specific method selection.
keywords:
  - exponential integrators
  - exponential Runge-Kutta methods
  - general linear methods
  - matrix functions
  - Krylov methods
  - Leja interpolation
  - scientific computing
authors:
  - family-names: "Villatoro"
    given-names: "Francisco R."
